  "question": {
    "text": "A rod of mass <math> <mi>M</mi> </math> and length <math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow> </math> is suspended at its middle by a wire. It exhibits torsional oscillations. If two masses, each of mass&nbsp;<math><mi>m</mi></math>, are attached at a distance <math> <mrow> <mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </math> from its centre on both sides, it reduces the oscillation frequency by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. The value of ratio <math><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></math> is close to"
  },
